# Downloaded model inputs and generated validation payloads.
/models
/build/
/build-*/
/dist/
/wheelhouse/
CMakeUserPresets.json
.idea/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Reproducible generated porting reports; committed intake records live under
# reports/porting/.
# No trailing slash: with one these match only directories, and a symlink is not
# a directory. Two of them were committed as symlinks holding an absolute
# workstation path, which a fresh clone resolves to nothing.
/reports/convert
/reports/reference
/reports/validate
/reports/bench

# reports/porting/ itself holds committed intake records (see above) and is
# NOT ignored wholesale, but scripts/convert-qwen3-tts.py's --report writes a
# large, mechanically-regenerable per-tensor conversion log into that same
# tree by convention (reports/porting/<family>/<variant>/convert.json). No
# convert.json has ever been committed in this project's history -- verified
# 2026-08-18 against every prior conversion, including CustomVoice's and
# Base's own -- which makes an untracked one sitting there an accident waiting
# for the next `git add -A` rather than a deliberate omission each time.
/reports/porting/**/convert.json

# The same hole, a second shape. scripts/dump_reference_qwen3_tts_voicedesign.py
# (Stage 3 Plan 1 Task 7) writes its captured oracle tensors under
# reports/porting/<family>/<variant>/oracle/ -- prefill.f32, codes.i32,
# waveform.f32, result.json -- rather than under build/goldens/..., which is
# where this family's other dumpers default and which /build/ above already
# ignores. That path was the plan's own instruction, not an accident, but the
# payload itself is exactly the golden-payload class docs/testing.md's
# "commit golden contracts, not golden payloads" rule refuses: several hundred
# KB of float32/int32 per case, mechanically regenerable from the checkpoint.
# Matches an entry NAMED "oracle" at ANY depth under reports/porting/: `**`
# spans zero or more directories, so reports/porting/oracle and
# reports/porting/<family>/<variant>/a/b/oracle both match, not only the
# <family>/<variant> depth the dumper actually writes. That breadth is the
# right direction for a rule whose whole job is surviving a stray
# `git add -A` -- the payload is mechanically regenerable from the
# checkpoint, so over-ignoring costs a regeneration and under-ignoring costs
# a committed golden payload. What keeps intake.json, tensor-inventory.json,
# _porting-log.md and friends committable is the NAME, not the depth: they
# are never named "oracle" at any level. (This comment claimed the narrower
# depth until 2026-08-19; `git check-ignore -v` disagreed with it.)
# No trailing slash, for the same symlink reason as the block above.
/reports/porting/**/oracle

# Agent scratch. Nothing here is a project artifact: it is whatever a session
# wrote while investigating. Added 2026-08-10 after `git add -A` swept 56 files
# and 9.0 MB of rate-sweep probes, WAVs and f32 dumps into a commit -- the
# reviewer that caught it was CodeRabbit, on files this project's own review
# never thought to look at.
.claude/
